<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - July 21.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - July 21.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended July 21</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     345	   1.54     632900  218.35   23.28</p>
<p>State Bank	   325	   1.41     540250  175.58   22.62</p>
<p>Telco		  385	   1.74     323700  124.62   23.57</p>
<p>TISCO		  200	   0.89     507650  101.53   23.20</p>
<p>Castrol		650	   2.89     120100   78.07   23.18</p>
<p>STERLITE	     235	   1.08     239800   56.35   23.96</p>
<p>SKF Bearing	 2355	 120.69	22100   52.05   66.81</p>
<p>Colgate		295	   1.32     162100   47.82   23.33</p>
<p>Reliance Cap	  69	   0.31     686600   47.38   23.43</p>
<p>Nestle		 270	   1.23     157600   42.55   23.75</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 25.75 percent on an annualised basis against 29.37 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 14.</p>
<p>Note :- BC - Book Closure</p>
